therapy (P less than 0.01). A reduction was observed in all Dukes\\\' stages. No significant difference between the     
treatment groups was observed with regard to frequency of distant metastases or overall survival. Among all randomized  
patients as well as the radically operated patients the recurrence-free interval, i.e., time to local recurrence or     
distant metastasis, was significantly prolonged in the preoperatively irradiated group. The radically operated patients 
